From: relay12 contributors
Subject: [PATCH] d3d11on12: replace MSVC pragmas and SDK-only crypto GUIDs

Three MinGW blockers, all in driver-side DDI code.

C4127 suppressions, at all 21 sites. Each suppresses MSVC's "conditional
expression is constant", which the ENTRYPOINT_END_REPORT_HR_AND_RETURN_VALUE
macro provokes. GCC has no such warning and rejects the pragma under
-Werror=unknown-pragmas. They now go through
RELAY_SUPPRESS_CONSTANT_CONDITIONAL, a _Pragma on MSVC and nothing elsewhere.

All 21 are converted, not the 4 the build reported. Compilation stops at the
first failing translation unit, so the other 17 were simply not reached yet;
fixing only what CI named would have moved the wall rather than removed it.

Bracketing the pragma with #ifdef/#endif would have been wrong:
`warning(suppress: n)` applies to the next line, so the #endif would sit
between it and the statement, and the suppression would quietly stop working
on the one compiler that needs it -- a regression nothing in this repository
could catch.

D3D11_DECODER_ENCRYPTION_HW_CENC and D3D11_KEY_EXCHANGE_HW_PROTECTION are
GUIDs the Windows SDK's d3d11.h declares and MinGW-w64's does not. They are
protocol GUIDs passed unchanged from the application through the runtime to
the driver, so the DDI header's names carry the same values. The DDI spelling
is also the more accurate one here rather than a workaround: these are DDI
entry points taking D3D10DDI_HDEVICE, and the line directly below the CENC
comparison already reads
D3DWDDM2_0DDI_VIDEO_DECODER_BEGIN_FRAME_CRYPTO_SESSION.

The rename is word-boundaried and excludes a trailing underscore, so
D3D11_KEY_EXCHANGE_HW_PROTECTION_DATA -- which MinGW does declare and which
this code also uses -- is untouched.
---
diff --git a/include/pch.hpp b/include/pch.hpp
index 7f902de..bf9c37a 100644
--- a/include/pch.hpp
+++ b/include/pch.hpp
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
 
 #include "SharedResourceHelpers.hpp"
 #include "relay_tracelogging.hpp"
+#include "relay_msvc_pragma.hpp"
 
 #ifndef __in
 #define __in _In_
diff --git a/src/VideoDecode.cpp b/src/VideoDecode.cpp
index 62cfdd8..134594f 100644
--- a/src/VideoDecode.cpp
+++ b/src/VideoDecode.cpp
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@ namespace D3D11On12
     {
         D3D11on12_DDI_ENTRYPOINT_START();
         const SIZE_T videoDecodeSize = sizeof(VideoDecode);
-#pragma warning( suppress : 4127 ) // conditional expression is constant
+RELAY_SUPPRESS_CONSTANT_CONDITIONAL // conditional expression is constant
         D3D11on12_DDI_ENTRYPOINT_END_REPORT_HR_AND_RETURN_VALUE(hDevice, S_OK, videoDecodeSize);
     }
 
@@ -146,7 +146,7 @@ namespace D3D11On12
             ZeroMemory(&m_inputArguments, sizeof(m_inputArguments));
             ZeroMemory(&m_outputArguments, sizeof(m_outputArguments));
 
-            if (m_bitstreamEncryption == D3D11_DECODER_ENCRYPTION_HW_CENC  &&  pVideoDecoderBeginFrame->ContentKeySize != sizeof(D3D11_VIDEO_DECODER_BEGIN_FRAME_CRYPTO_SESSION))
+            if (m_bitstreamEncryption == D3DWDDM2_0DDI_DECODER_ENCRYPTION_HW_CENC  &&  pVideoDecoderBeginFrame->ContentKeySize != sizeof(D3D11_VIDEO_DECODER_BEGIN_FRAME_CRYPTO_SESSION))
             {
                 const D3DWDDM2_0DDI_VIDEO_DECODER_BEGIN_FRAME_CRYPTO_SESSION *pBeginFrameCryptoSession = static_cast<const D3DWDDM2_0DDI_VIDEO_DECODER_BEGIN_FRAME_CRYPTO_SESSION *>(pVideoDecoderBeginFrame->pContentKey);
                 m_inputArguments.DecryptionArguments.pKeyInfo = pBeginFrameCryptoSession->pBlob;
